<span>Postal Service Analogy:
</span></span><span>
</span><span>=F0=9F=93=AC GET (Reading Mail):
</span><span>- Look in mailbox without changing anything
</span><span>- Can peek multiple times safely
</span><span>- Postman logs who checked what
</span><span>- Fast because no processing needed
</span><span>
</span><span>=F0=9F=93=AE POST (Sending Letter):
</span><span>- Create new mail item
</span><span>- Each letter is unique delivery
</span><span>- Requires proper address/postage
</span><span>- Processing time varies
</span><span>
</span><span>=F0=9F=93=A6 PUT (Package Replacement):
</span><span>- Replace entire package contents
</span><span>- Same result if sent multiple times
</span><span>- Requires full new package
</span><span>
</span><span>=F0=9F=94=A7 PATCH (Package Repair):
</span><span>- Fix specific part of package
</span><span>- Might have different result if repeated
</span><span>- Targeted modification
</span><span>
</span><span>=F0=9F=97=91=EF=B8=8F DELETE (Mail Removal):
</span><span>- Remove item from system
</span><span>- Same result if repeated (already gone)
</span><span>- Permanent action
</span><span>
</span><span>=E2=9D=93 OPTIONS (Service Inquiry):
</span><span>- Ask what services available
</span><span>- Get information about capabilities
</span><span>- No actual mail processing</span></code></pre></div></div>
